    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "items": [
        {
          "q": "What does a BMW cylinder head rebuild include?",
          "a": "It includes removal, full strip-down, inspection, head resurfacing (skimming), valve grinding or replacement, new valve stem seals, seat recutting, VANOS service (where applicable), reassembly with new gaskets and seals, and final testing."
        },
        {
          "q": "How long does cylinder head repair take?",
          "a": "Typical turnaround is 3–5 working days, depending on the extent of machining required and parts availability. We will give you a clear timeline when you bring your vehicle in."
        },
        {
          "q": "Do you service VANOS during the head rebuild?",
          "a": "Yes, for all BMW engines with VANOS (most modern models), we service the unit as part of the cylinder head overhaul to ensure correct variable valve timing and engine performance."
        },
        {
          "q": "Is the cylinder head skimmed on every rebuild?",
          "a": "We always measure the head for warpage. If it is out of specification, we resurface it to restore a perfectly flat sealing surface. This is a standard part of our process."
        },
        {
          "q": "What warranty do you offer on cylinder head work?",
          "a": "All cylinder head rebuilds come with a 12-month unlimited-mileage warranty covering parts and labour."
        }
      ]
    }
